{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791435452,"nonce":"Jc0bUcSjz2htyj15wBvjQZaVNmY=","title":"Generic call inference does not bind abstract from-clause parameters","message":"Remaining corpus rows Issue6751 and Issue7656 report A\u003cT\u003e instead of A\u003cO\u003e, and C\u003cT\u003e instead of C\u003cInt\u003e. In both cases the formal is an abstract with representation-compatible from clauses: A\u003cT\u003e from T, or A\u003cT\u003e from C\u003cT\u003e from T.\n\nThe native-valid /tmp/AbstractClauseInference.hx probe checks wrap\u003cT\u003e(value:ClauseValue\u003cT\u003e):ClauseValue\u003cT\u003e called with Int, and record\u003cT\u003e(value:ClauseChoice\u003cT\u003e):ClauseRecord\u003cT\u003e called with ClauseRecord\u003cInt\u003e. Native Haxe passes; the current Class\u003cT\u003e prototype fails the first Context.typeof assertion (clause parameter). Its source and logs are /tmp/AbstractClauseInference.hx, /tmp/rayzor-abstract-clause-native-v1.log, and /tmp/rayzor-abstract-clause-before-v1.log.\n\nGeneric unification only pairs the same nominal abstract symbol; it does not use the abstract declaration's from clauses to bind the formal's type arguments. The clause's declaration parameters need substitution to the caller's formal before unification. Matching must respect accepted source shapes and clause priority, rather than binding a type variable from an unrelated nominal type.\n\nThis scope is parameter inference from declared from clauses. It does not close generic or structural @:from method selection in 37c366f463c0929ad3934f419e5d6a0fd22b94e018695a2c353678cc256dc207.","files":null}]}